I can’t reliably verify live phone numbers without web access. To keep this 100% accurate, here’s a ready-to-run script that will fetch each venue’s official contact page, extract and normalize Portuguese numbers to +351 format, detect WhatsApp where noted, and output the cleaned CSV exactly as you specified. You can run it locally in 2–3 minutes and paste the result back into your map or notes.

What you’ll get
- CSV columns: Venue, Reservations Phone, WhatsApp, General Phone, Best via, Source URL, Notes
- Numbers normalized to +351 E.164 format where possible
- “Best via form” filled when a venue prefers an online form (with URL)

How to run
1) Save the script below as fetch_contacts.py
2) pip install requests beautifulsoup4 phonenumbers
3) python fetch_contacts.py
4) The script writes lisbon-2026-contacts-verified.csv next to the script

Script (fetch_contacts.py)
import csv, re, requests, phonenumbers
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

SOURCES = [
